# No credentials or secrets

Never add secrets or private material to this repository (tracked files, commits, docs, examples, or configs).

## Do not commit or invent

- Passwords, API keys, tokens, cookies, session IDs
- Private keys, certificates, `.pem` / `.key` / `.p12` / WireGuard keys
- VPN / Wi-Fi configs with secrets (`.ovpn`, `wg*.conf` with `PrivateKey`, NetworkManager connection dumps)
- `.env` files or hardcoded env secrets
- Real hostnames/IPs tied to private infrastructure when avoidable
- Personal emails or phone numbers beyond the public GitHub noreply author in `pyproject.toml`

## Prefer instead

- Read secrets at runtime from the OS (NetworkManager, secret stores, env vars the user already has)
- Use placeholders in docs: `YOUR_TOKEN`, `/path/to/config.ovpn`
- Keep example configs free of real credentials

## If asked to add a secret

Refuse to write it into the repo. Point at OS/keyring/`nmcli` / env vars instead.
